Package: com.heavenzy.tweak
Name: Heavenzy
Version: 1.9.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Per-app device identity reset (Blaze-style): keeps your real iPhone model but resets serial, UDID, IDFV, IDFA, Wi-Fi/Bluetooth MAC and IMEI, plus a wipe + re-spoof that clears saved accounts and blocks iCloud restore, so an app sees a brand-new phone with a first-time install. Hold two fingers on any app to open the draggable Kairos panel (touches pass through around it): inside Instagram it scans the visible usernames (Scan, scroll, scan again, Copy). An optional Approved Names list keeps only accounts whose display-name first name matches, and Auto scan taps Scan every second so you just scroll. Close the panel with its X. Each app also has an App Data & Tools screen (AppData-style): view version, build, sizes and containers, open the bundle/data/group folders in Filza, copy the bundle id, clear caches, reset data, reset permissions, offload, or open the App Store page, plus rename the home-screen icon and set a badge count (applied by the SpringBoard hook). Configure each app and the scraper from the Heavenzy app; no account or sign-in is required.
Maintainer: Heavenzy
Author: Heavenzy
Section: Tweaks
Depends: ellekit, com.opa334.libsandy
